' F5 -- Conceptual domain model.
' Chapter 3 (Requirements). UML class diagram.
' Claim supported: the domain vocabulary and its multiplicities, at analysis
' level. Deliberately distinct from F9 (the physical ER schema) -- this one
' names concepts, including one (Quiz) that has no table behind it.
@startuml f5-domain-model
!include _style.iuml

title Conceptual domain model

hide methods
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class User {
  role : student | professor | admin
}
class Course
class Lecture {
  visibility : course | private_student
}
class Slide {
  slideNumber
  needsReview
}
class Quiz <<derived>> #DCDCDC
class Question {
  options[4]
  correctAnswer
}
class Concept
class Embedding {
  vector : 768
}

class Attempt <<abstract>>
class QuizAttempt
class ExamAttempt
class ReviewGrade {
  rating : 1..4
}

User "1" -- "0..*" Course : owns >
User "0..*" -- "0..*" Course : enrolled in >
Course "1" -- "0..*" Lecture : contains >
Lecture "1" -- "1..*" Slide : contains >
Slide "1" -- "0..*" Question : tests >
Lecture "1" -- "0..*" Embedding : vectorised as >
Slide "0..*" -- "0..*" Concept : teaches >

Quiz .. Slide : "//derived//: the set of\nQuestions reachable via\nSlide.lecture"

Attempt <|-- QuizAttempt
Attempt <|-- ExamAttempt
Attempt <|-- ReviewGrade
User "1" -- "0..*" Attempt : performs >
Question "1" -- "0..*" Attempt : answered in >

note right of Quiz
  **No Quiz table exists.**
  A quiz is implicit — the set of
  quiz_questions joined through
  slides.lecture_id. Modelled here
  because it is real domain
  vocabulary, but it must not appear
  as an entity in F9.
end note

note bottom of Concept
  Concept and its links are **write-idle by default**:
  ingestion is gated behind FEATURE_COURSE_BRAIN (off),
  so in a default deployment no Slide teaches any Concept.
  That single default also empties concept mastery — see F17.
end note

legend bottom
  Analysis-level model: names the domain, not the tables. Compare F9, which shows the
  26 physical tables actually deployed, three unenforced relationships, and the four
  dead tables excluded from it.
endlegend

@enduml
